Marble cake with chocolate and custard
6
Vanilla-chocolate marble cake served with vanilla custard.

---
Marble cake
eggs|300|g
wheat flour|250|g
soft butter|250|g
powdered sugar|250|g
vanilla sugar|15|g
baking powder|6|g
unsweetened cocoa powder|50|g

Tins
soft butter|30|g
wheat flour|30|g

Custard
semi-skimmed milk|250|ml
egg yolks|40|g
powdered sugar|40|g
vanilla pod|1|pcs

---
Make the cake: preheat the oven to 210°C.
Cream the softened butter with the sugars until smooth.
Add the whole eggs 2 by 2, whisking well.
Add the flour and baking powder sifted together, mix until combined.
Divide the batter in half.
Add the cocoa to one half and mix.

Butter and flour a loaf tin.
Fill the tin alternating layers of plain and cocoa batter.
Run a spoon handle through in a zigzag to marble.
Bake about 40 min at 210°C (or 20 min less for individual tins).
Let cool 15 min then turn out onto a rack.

Make the custard: bring the milk to the boil with the split and scraped vanilla pod.
Whisk the egg yolks with the sugar.
Pour the boiling milk over the yolk mixture while whisking.
Return to low heat and stir until it coats the back of a spoon (about 84°C, do not exceed).
Strain and cool quickly (e.g. over an ice bath).

---
To check the custard: draw a line on the spoon — if the edges stay clear, it is ready.
Adjust oven temperature to your tin size and type.
Serve the cake slightly warm with cold custard.

---
dessert
cake
marble
chocolate
custard
